      "settings": {
        "bundled": "svc-adas",
        "image_alt": "",
        "tag": "What ADAS is",
        "heading": "Your car's cameras have to see straight.",
        "highlight": "see straight.",
        "text": "ADAS stands for advanced driver-assistance systems: lane keeping, lane departure warning, automatic emergency braking and adaptive cruise control. Many of these rely on a camera mounted behind the windshield. When the windshield is replaced, the camera has to be recalibrated so it reads the road where the road really is. Geaux Auto Glass recalibrates ADAS on cars, SUVs and trucks. Tell us the year, make and model when you request a quote and we will confirm what your vehicle needs.",
        "link_label": "",
        "link": "",
        "ground": "paper",
        "anchor_id": ""
      }
    },
