    "faq": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "question1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is ADAS recalibration?",
            "answer": "<p>Setting a vehicle's driver-assist camera back to the position and aim it was built for, so features like lane keeping and automatic emergency braking read the road correctly.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need it after a windshield replacement?",
            "answer": "<p>If your vehicle has a driver-assist camera mounted on the windshield, usually yes: the new glass changes what the camera sees. Tell us the year, make and model and we will confirm. <a href=\"/pages/windshield-replacement\">About windshield replacement</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Which vehicles do you recalibrate?",
            "answer": "<p>Cars, SUVs and trucks, domestic and foreign.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How soon can you do it?",
            "answer": "<p>Same day or next day. We work by appointment, so call or request a quote to get on the schedule.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question5": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does insurance cover ADAS recalibration?",
            "answer": "<p>Comprehensive coverage covers glass damage. When recalibration is part of a windshield claim, ask your insurance to confirm it is included when you call to start the filing with the company name Geaux Auto Glass.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
